  "releaseNotes": "PickArgmin: drop `[<Literal>]` from `ResultFloats`. A literal in a `[<ReflectedDefinition>]` module compiles to a const field with no backing property, which poisons `Expr.TryGetReflectedDefinition` for EVERY method in the assembly — so heap-pick `Normal24.encode` (and any reflected function) became \"not reflectable\". Plain `let` = a bindable property.",
